Part 1 — Linux Fundamentals

Learned the basics of the Linux command line, including navigating the filesystem, listing and searching files, using commands with flags, and accessing command documentation through --help and man pages.

Key commands: ls, cd, pwd, find, grep, cat, man

Part 2 — Linux Fundamentals

Learned how to manage files and directories, understand Linux permissions and ownership, switch between users, and explore important system directories.

Key commands: touch, mkdir, cp, mv, rm, file, chmod, su

